    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">small cytoplasmic RNA (scRNA)</rdfs:label>
    <dcterms:description xml:lang="en">A small cytoplasmic RNA (scRNA) molecule is a small (7S; 129 nucleotides) RNA molecule found in the cytosol and rough endoplasmic reticulum that are normally associated with proteins that are involved in specific selection and transport of other proteins.</dcterms:description>
